{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_WO-SWOF-W2-002_SPEC.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_WO-SWOF-W2-002_SPEC.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# WO-SWOF-W2-002 SPEC — SWOF effect / observation / UNKNOWN_EFFECT / reconciliation substrate\n\nYou are the tracked mutation writer for SWOF WorkOrder `WO-SWOF-W2-002`.\nYou may write ONLY the files listed in section 1. Writing any other path is a governance violation.\n\nHard rules:\n- Python 3.11+, standard library ONLY. ASCII only. LF endings.\n- No live effect: every function here works on local/simulated fixtures. Never perform a network call,\n  a subprocess, a filesystem effect, or a broker/business action. The substrate is a STATE MACHINE\n  over records, not an executor.\n- The central law of this WorkOrder: **a provider/tool response is an OBSERVATION, never world-state\n  truth.** Only a readback that matches the intended effect may reach `RECONCILED`. Uncertainty is\n  `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`, which is a first-class terminal state, not an error to be retried away.\n- Fail closed. Typed exceptions with the exact `code` attributes below. Never `except: pass`.\n- Deterministic: no wall-clock in a decision; accept `now`/`clock` as an injected parameter.\n\n## 1. Exact file list (create every one)\n\n```\nsrc/effect/__init__.py\nsrc/effect/README.md\nsrc/effect/state.py\nsrc/effect/substrate.py\nsrc/effect/idempotency.py\nsrc/effect/compensation.py\nsrc/effect/correlation.py\nsrc/effect/tests/__init__.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_state.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_substrate.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_idempotency.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_compensation.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_correlation.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_adversarial.py\nschemas/effect/README.md\nschemas/effect/effect_record.schema.json\n```\n\nTests use the repository convention:\n\n```python\nimport sys, unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"src\"))\nfrom effect.state import ...   # noqa: E402\n```\n\nEvery test lives INSIDE a `unittest.TestCase` class; the module ends with\n`if __name__ == \"__main__\": unittest.main()` and no test is defined after it.\n\n## 2. Required API and behaviour\n\n### 2.1 `src/effect/state.py`\n\n```python\nINTENT_STATES   = (\"INTENDED\", \"ATTEMPTED\", \"OBSERVED\", \"READBACK\")\nTERMINAL_STATES = (\"RECONCILED\", \"UNKNOWN_EFFECT\", \"PARTIAL_EFFECT\", \"DENIED\", \"FAILED\",\n                   \"COMPENSATED\", \"IRREVERSIBLE\")\nEFFECT_STATES   = INTENT_STATES + TERMINAL_STATES\n\nclass EffectTransitionRefused(Exception): code = \"ERR_EFFECT_TRANSITION_REFUSED\"\n\nALLOWED_TRANSITIONS: dict[str, frozenset[str]]\ndef is_terminal(state) -> bool\ndef is_unknown(state) -> bool               # True for UNKNOWN_EFFECT and PARTIAL_EFFECT\ndef assert_transition(src, dst) -> tuple[str, str]   # raises EffectTransitionRefused\ndef state_rank(state) -> int                # stable rank for deterministic ordering\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. Unknown state names raise `EffectTransitionRefused` (fail closed) even for a query.\n2. `OBSERVED -> RECONCILED` is NOT an allowed transition: `OBSERVED -> READBACK -> RECONCILED` is the\n   only path to truth. `assert_transition(\"OBSERVED\", \"RECONCILED\")` must raise.\n3. `DENIED` is reachable only from `INTENDED` (a permission refusal happens before any attempt).\n4. Every terminal state rejects all further transitions except `PARTIAL_EFFECT -> COMPENSATED`.\n\n### 2.2 `src/effect/substrate.py`\n\n```python\nclass EffectDenied(Exception):        code = \"ERR_EFFECT_DENIED\"\nclass EffectStateError(Exception):    code = \"ERR_EFFECT_STATE\"\nclass SuccessInferenceRefused(Exception): code = \"ERR_SUCCESS_INFERENCE_REFUSED\"\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Attempt: actor: str; attempt_key: str; at: str\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Observation: payload: object; provider_success: bool | None; at: str\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Readback: payload: object; matches_expected: bool | None; at: str; stale: bool = False\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass EffectRecord:\n    effect_id: str; subject_id: str; intent: object; intent_digest: str\n    state: str; attempts: tuple[Attempt, ...] = (); observations: tuple[Observation, ...] = ()\n    readbacks: tuple[Readback, ...] = (); provider_success: bool | None = None\n    reason_code: str = \"\"; correlation_id: str = \"\"; environment: str = \"local\"\n\ndef intend(effect_id, subject_id, intent, *, environment=\"local\") -> EffectRecord\ndef record_attempt(record, *, actor, permission_allowed, attempt_key, at) -> EffectRecord\ndef observe(record, *, payload, provider_success, at) -> EffectRecord\ndef readback(record, *, payload, expected, at, stale=False) -> EffectRecord\ndef reconcile(record, *, at) -> EffectRecord\ndef finalize(record) -> EffectRecord\ndef assert_no_success_inference(record) -> None   # raises SuccessInferenceRefused\ndef is_success(record) -> bool                    # True ONLY for RECONCILED\n```\n\nLaws (each is a required test):\n1. `record_attempt(permission_allowed=False)` returns a record in `DENIED` with\n   `reason_code=\"PERMISSION_DENIED\"` and records NO attempt. `assert_no_success_inference` then raises\n   `SuccessInferenceRefused` if anyone asks for success.\n2. `observe(provider_success=True)` moves `ATTEMPTED -> OBSERVED` and stores the payload, but the\n   record is NOT success: `is_success` is False and the state is `OBSERVED`, never `RECONCILED`.\n3. `reconcile` requires at least one readback with `matches_expected is True` AND `stale is False`.\n   - no readback => `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`, `reason_code=\"NO_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED\"`.\n   - stale readback only => `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`, `reason_code=\"STALE_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED\"`.\n   - readback present but `matches_expected is None` (ambiguous) => `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`,\n     `reason_code=\"AMBIGUOUS_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED\"`.\n   - readback `matches_expected is False` => `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`, `reason_code=\"RECONCILIATION_MISMATCH\"`.\n   - some but not all expected sub-effects matched => `PARTIAL_EFFECT`,\n     `reason_code=\"PARTIAL_EFFECT_DETECTED\"`.\n   - all expected matched, fresh => `RECONCILED`.\n4. `finalize` is the fail-closed sweep: it converts any non-terminal record into `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`\n   with `reason_code=\"UNRESOLVED_EFFECT_FAIL_CLOSED\"`, and any `OBSERVED` record whose provider said\n   success but which has no readback into `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` with `NO_READBACK_AFTER_PROVIDER_SUCCESS`.\n   `finalize` must NEVER raise and must never return a success state it cannot justify.\n5. `assert_no_success_inference(record)` raises `SuccessInferenceRefused` unless the record is\n   `RECONCILED`; it also raises when `provider_success is True` and the state is not `RECONCILED`.\n6. `readback` on a record whose subject differs from the request's subject is refused with\n   `EffectStateError` and `reason_code=\"WRONG_SUBJECT_READBACK\"`.\n7. the intent digest is over immutable semantic content only (effect_id, subject_id, intent); it must\n   not change when the record is later mutated by attempts/observations.\n\n### 2.3 `src/effect/idempotency.py`\n\n```python\nclass DuplicateAttemptDetected(Exception): code = \"ERR_DUPLICATE_ATTEMPT\"\nclass RetryRefused(Exception):             code = \"ERR_RETRY_REFUSED\"\n\ndef attempt_key(effect_id, subject_id, intent_digest, attempt_no) -> str    # deterministic sha256 hex\ndef classify_retry(record, *, attempt_no) -> str   # \"NEW\" | \"DUPLICATE\" | \"REFUSED\"\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass RetryPlan: allowed: bool; next_attempt_no: int; reason_code: str; idempotency_key: str\ndef plan_retry(record, *, max_retries=3) -> RetryPlan\ndef assert_retryable(record, *, attempt_no, max_retries=3) -> RetryPlan   # raises\ndef plan_reobserve(record) -> dict   # {\"reobserve\": bool, \"reason_code\": ...}\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. the same `attempt_no` for the same (effect, subject, intent) yields the same key, and a second\n   attempt with an existing key raises `DuplicateAttemptDetected` (no duplicate side effect).\n2. retry is refused (`RetryRefused`) for any terminal state except `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` and\n   `PARTIAL_EFFECT`; retrying a `RECONCILED` effect, a `DENIED` effect or an `IRREVERSIBLE` effect is\n   refused with a typed reason.\n3. `max_retries` is a hard ceiling: exceeding it refuses rather than looping.\n4. `plan_reobserve` asks for a fresh readback (never a new side effect) for `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` and\n   `PARTIAL_EFFECT`.\n\n### 2.4 `src/effect/compensation.py`\n\n```python\nclass IrreversibleEffect(Exception):   code = \"ERR_IRREVERSIBLE_EFFECT\"\nclass NoCompensationPath(Exception):   code = \"ERR_NO_COMPENSATION_PATH\"\n\nCOMPENSABLE_KINDS = (\"COMPENSATE\", \"ROLLBACK\")\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CompensationPointer:\n    target_effect_id: str; ref: str; kind: str; compensable: bool; reason_code: str\n\ndef classify(record, *, irreversible_attempts=()) -> str\ndef plan_compensation(record, *, registry=None, irreversible_attempts=()) -> CompensationPointer\ndef assert_compensable(pointer) -> CompensationPointer\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. an effect with any declared irreversible attempt classifies as `IRREVERSIBLE`, and\n   `plan_compensation` returns a pointer with `compensable=False` and\n   `reason_code=\"IRREVERSIBLE_EFFECT\"`; `assert_compensable` then raises `IrreversibleEffect`.\n2. a `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with a registered compensation path returns a `COMPENSATE`/`ROLLBACK` pointer.\n3. a `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with no registered path raises `NoCompensationPath` — an explicit refusal rather\n   than a silent pass.\n4. compensation is planned, never executed here; the pointer carries an exact `ref`.\n\n### 2.5 `src/effect/correlation.py`\n\n```python\nclass WrongSubjectEvidence(Exception):  code = \"ERR_WRONG_SUBJECT_EVIDENCE\"\nclass CorrelationMismatch(Exception):   code = \"ERR_CORRELATION_MISMATCH\"\n\ndef correlation_id(effect_id, subject_id, intent_digest, environment) -> str\ndef bind_evidence(record, evidence_ref, *, evidence_subject_id, evidence_correlation_id) -> dict\ndef verify_correlation(record, evidence) -> dict   # {\"bound\": bool, \"reason_code\": str}\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. `correlation_id` is deterministic and depends on all four inputs; changing any input changes it.\n2. `bind_evidence` raises `WrongSubjectEvidence` when the evidence subject differs from the record's\n   subject, and `CorrelationMismatch` when the correlation id differs.\n3. the returned binding carries `effect_id`, `subject_id`, `correlation_id`, `evidence_ref` and\n   `subject_match: True` — the exact effect/evidence correlation identity the evidence pack needs.\n\n## 3. Schema\n\n`schemas/effect/effect_record.schema.json` (draft 2020-12, `$id`\n`https://swof.local/schemas/effect/effect_record.schema.json`, `additionalProperties: false`):\nrequired `effect_id`, `subject_id`, `state`, `intent_digest`, `environment`; `state` an enum of the\nfull `EFFECT_STATES` list; `provider_success` a boolean or null; `readbacks` an array of objects with\n`matches_expected` boolean-or-null and `stale` boolean; plus `reason_code`, `correlation_id`.\n`schemas/effect/README.md` documents the observation-vs-truth law.\n\n## 4. Required adversarial tests (at least 35 across the files)\n\nEach asserts its exact typed error or terminal state:\n1. apparent success with no readback -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `NO_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED`.\n2. ambiguous provider response (provider_success None) + readback pending -> stays `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`.\n3. duplicate retry -> `DuplicateAttemptDetected`.\n4. partial effect -> `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with a compensation pointer.\n5. stale readback -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `STALE_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED`.\n6. wrong-subject readback -> `EffectStateError` / `WRONG_SUBJECT_READBACK`.\n7. reconciliation mismatch -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `RECONCILIATION_MISMATCH`.\n8. denied permission -> `DENIED`, no attempt recorded, `assert_no_success_inference` raises.\n9. `assert_transition(\"OBSERVED\", \"RECONCILED\")` raises `EffectTransitionRefused`.\n10. irreversible effect -> `IrreversibleEffect` from `assert_compensable`.\n11. retry of a `RECONCILED` effect -> `RetryRefused`.\n12. `finalize` never returns a success state without a matching readback.\n\n## 5. Definition of done\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s src/effect/tests -t src/effect/tests` reports OK with the full count.\nDo not modify any path outside `src/effect/**` and `schemas/effect/**`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
