{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_WO-SWOF-W2-002_SPEC.md'; (Get-Content -LiteralPath \"'$p)[145..231] -join \"`n\"; Write-Output \"=====PYPROJECT=====\"; Get-Content C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\SWOF\\\\pyproject.toml -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"def plan_reobserve(record) -> dict   # {\"reobserve\": bool, \"reason_code\": ...}\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. the same `attempt_no` for the same (effect, subject, intent) yields the same key, and a second\n   attempt with an existing key raises `DuplicateAttemptDetected` (no duplicate side effect).\n2. retry is refused (`RetryRefused`) for any terminal state except `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` and\n   `PARTIAL_EFFECT`; retrying a `RECONCILED` effect, a `DENIED` effect or an `IRREVERSIBLE` effect is\n   refused with a typed reason.\n3. `max_retries` is a hard ceiling: exceeding it refuses rather than looping.\n4. `plan_reobserve` asks for a fresh readback (never a new side effect) for `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` and\n   `PARTIAL_EFFECT`.\n\n### 2.4 `src/effect/compensation.py`\n\n```python\nclass IrreversibleEffect(Exception):   code = \"ERR_IRREVERSIBLE_EFFECT\"\nclass NoCompensationPath(Exception):   code = \"ERR_NO_COMPENSATION_PATH\"\n\nCOMPENSABLE_KINDS = (\"COMPENSATE\", \"ROLLBACK\")\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CompensationPointer:\n    target_effect_id: str; ref: str; kind: str; compensable: bool; reason_code: str\n\ndef classify(record, *, irreversible_attempts=()) -> str\ndef plan_compensation(record, *, registry=None, irreversible_attempts=()) -> CompensationPointer\ndef assert_compensable(pointer) -> CompensationPointer\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. an effect with any declared irreversible attempt classifies as `IRREVERSIBLE`, and\n   `plan_compensation` returns a pointer with `compensable=False` and\n   `reason_code=\"IRREVERSIBLE_EFFECT\"`; `assert_compensable` then raises `IrreversibleEffect`.\n2. a `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with a registered compensation path returns a `COMPENSATE`/`ROLLBACK` pointer.\n3. a `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with no registered path raises `NoCompensationPath` — an explicit refusal rather\n   than a silent pass.\n4. compensation is planned, never executed here; the pointer carries an exact `ref`.\n\n### 2.5 `src/effect/correlation.py`\n\n```python\nclass WrongSubjectEvidence(Exception):  code = \"ERR_WRONG_SUBJECT_EVIDENCE\"\nclass CorrelationMismatch(Exception):   code = \"ERR_CORRELATION_MISMATCH\"\n\ndef correlation_id(effect_id, subject_id, intent_digest, environment) -> str\ndef bind_evidence(record, evidence_ref, *, evidence_subject_id, evidence_correlation_id) -> dict\ndef verify_correlation(record, evidence) -> dict   # {\"bound\": bool, \"reason_code\": str}\n```\n\nLaws:\n1. `correlation_id` is deterministic and depends on all four inputs; changing any input changes it.\n2. `bind_evidence` raises `WrongSubjectEvidence` when the evidence subject differs from the record's\n   subject, and `CorrelationMismatch` when the correlation id differs.\n3. the returned binding carries `effect_id`, `subject_id`, `correlation_id`, `evidence_ref` and\n   `subject_match: True` — the exact effect/evidence correlation identity the evidence pack needs.\n\n## 3. Schema\n\n`schemas/effect/effect_record.schema.json` (draft 2020-12, `$id`\n`https://swof.local/schemas/effect/effect_record.schema.json`, `additionalProperties: false`):\nrequired `effect_id`, `subject_id`, `state`, `intent_digest`, `environment`; `state` an enum of the\nfull `EFFECT_STATES` list; `provider_success` a boolean or null; `readbacks` an array of objects with\n`matches_expected` boolean-or-null and `stale` boolean; plus `reason_code`, `correlation_id`.\n`schemas/effect/README.md` documents the observation-vs-truth law.\n\n## 4. Required adversarial tests (at least 35 across the files)\n\nEach asserts its exact typed error or terminal state:\n1. apparent success with no readback -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `NO_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED`.\n2. ambiguous provider response (provider_success None) + readback pending -> stays `UNKNOWN_EFFECT`.\n3. duplicate retry -> `DuplicateAttemptDetected`.\n4. partial effect -> `PARTIAL_EFFECT` with a compensation pointer.\n5. stale readback -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `STALE_READBACK_FAIL_CLOSED`.\n6. wrong-subject readback -> `EffectStateError` / `WRONG_SUBJECT_READBACK`.\n7. reconciliation mismatch -> `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` / `RECONCILIATION_MISMATCH`.\n8. denied permission -> `DENIED`, no attempt recorded, `assert_no_success_inference` raises.\n9. `assert_transition(\"OBSERVED\", \"RECONCILED\")` raises `EffectTransitionRefused`.\n10. irreversible effect -> `IrreversibleEffect` from `assert_compensable`.\n11. retry of a `RECONCILED` effect -> `RetryRefused`.\n12. `finalize` never returns a success state without a matching readback.\n\n## 5. Definition of done\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s src/effect/tests -t src/effect/tests` reports OK with the full count.\nDo not modify any path outside `src/effect/**` and `schemas/effect/**`.\r\n=====PYPROJECT=====\r\n[project]\r\nname = \"swof\"\r\nversion = \"0.0.0\"\r\ndescription = \"SWOF / SWOF GENIE - construction under HG-KSEOS governance\"\r\nrequires-python = \">=3.11\"\r\ndependencies = []\r\n\r\n# W0-002 exit: the repository skeleton must use a STDLIB test runner so the bootstrap\r\n# is verifiable without adding a dependency (defect W0-002-TR-001).\r\n[tool.swof]\r\ntest_runner = \"python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .\"\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
